{"uid":"a96a5326314b3788","name":"test_a_mix_of_curable_and_incurable_gate_findings_still_ends_the_run","fullName":"tests.test_peer_verdict_gate#test_a_mix_of_curable_and_incurable_gate_findings_still_ends_the_run","historyId":"303ff2cbd0b1575cc7667e601297660c","time":{"start":1791867007981,"stop":1791867008141,"duration":160},"description":"Task 003 (PRD requirement A.3): the complement `_gate_cure_pass_\n    available`'s own docstring names -- a rejection carrying even one\n    non-curable blocking finding beside an otherwise-curable one never\n    takes the cure-pass edge (`findings.all_blocking_findings_curable`\n    requires the WHOLE blocking set, review's own mirror is\n    `test_a_mix_of_curable_and_incurable_findings_never_takes_the_cure_\n    pass` in `tests/test_cure_pass.py`), so this falls straight through to\n    the ordinary archive/replan-or-finish edges below, ending the run\n    exactly as it always has -- A.1 is never a claim that the gate can no\n    longer fail a run. Driven end to end through `_run_job_core()` (never\n    `_step_verdict_gate` in isolation) on the `test020-verdict-gate`\n    fixture (`_supervisor` above) with `max_approaches=1` -- the LAST\n    approach -- so a wrongly-taken cure pass would be the only thing\n    standing between this mixed rejection and a terminal `failed` state.\n\n    Task cure-01-01-3 (PRD requirement A.3's removal-specific review\n    rule): this last-approach case must reach that terminal state by the\n    SAME `verdict_gate_rejected_on_merits` edge the approach-left case\n    takes (`..._ends_the_run_with_an_approach_left` below), so the\n    archive/composite-PRD absences are asserted here too. Before that\n    task's fix the `approach < max_approaches` guard let the last approach\n    alone fall through to the ordinary archive/replan-or-finish edges,\n    which archived approach 1 under `approaches/01/` and wrote a\n    `composite-prd.md` nothing downstream ever read -- this test passed\n    anyway, because it never looked.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 003 (PRD requirement A.3): the complement <code>_gate_cure_pass_ available</code>'s own docstring names -- a rejection carrying even one<br />\nnon-curable blocking finding beside an otherwise-curable one never<br />\ntakes the cure-pass edge (<code>findings.all_blocking_findings_curable</code><br />\nrequires the WHOLE blocking set, review's own mirror is<br />\n<code>test_a_mix_of_curable_and_incurable_findings_never_takes_the_cure_ pass</code> in <code>tests/test_cure_pass.py</code>), so this falls straight through to<br />\nthe ordinary archive/replan-or-finish edges below, ending the run<br />\nexactly as it always has -- A.1 is never a claim that the gate can no<br />\nlonger fail a run. Driven end to end through <code>_run_job_core()</code> (never<br />\n<code>_step_verdict_gate</code> in isolation) on the <code>test020-verdict-gate</code><br />\nfixture (<code>_supervisor</code> above) with <code>max_approaches=1</code> -- the LAST<br />\napproach -- so a wrongly-taken cure pass would be the only thing<br />\nstanding between this mixed rejection and a terminal <code>failed</code> state.</p>\n<pre><code>Task cure-01-01-3 (PRD requirement A.3's removal-specific review\nrule): this last-approach case must reach that terminal state by the\nSAME `verdict_gate_rejected_on_merits` edge the approach-left case\ntakes (`..._ends_the_run_with_an_approach_left` below), so the\narchive/composite-PRD absences are asserted here too. Before that\ntask's fix the `approach &lt; max_approaches` guard let the last approach\nalone fall through to the ordinary archive/replan-or-finish edges,\nwhich archived approach 1 under `approaches/01/` and wrote a\n`composite-prd.md` nothing downstream ever read -- this test passed\nanyway, because it never looked.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791866910604,"stop":1791866910605,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791866910605,"stop":1791866910605,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791867007966,"stop":1791867007970,"duration":4},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791867007966,"stop":1791867007966,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791867007970,"stop":1791867007974,"duration":4},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791867007970,"stop":1791867007970,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_escalation_backoff_at_class_level","time":{"start":1791867007975,"stop":1791867007975,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_stub_wait_out_backoff_at_class_level","time":{"start":1791867007975,"stop":1791867007975,"duration":0},"s